{
  "id": "u03-l05",
  "unit": "u03-family",
  "title": "I have…",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Bengali has no verb 'to have'. You say **'to me there is'**: **আমার একটা বোন আছে** (*amar ekta bon achhe*), literally 'My one sister exists' = 'I have a sister.' It's **আমার**, not আমি. Negative: **আমার ভাই নেই** 'I have no brother.' Question: **তোমার কি ভাই আছে?**\n\n**একটা** = 'a / one (thing)'. Plural 'our / your': আমরা → **আমাদের**, তোমরা → **তোমাদের**.\n\nHusband and wife: **স্বামী** (*shami*) and **স্ত্রী** (*stri*) are neutral; in everyday speech many people say **বউ** (*bou*) for 'wife' (it also means 'bride').",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "ekta",
      "bn": "একটা",
      "tr": "ekta",
      "en": "one; a",
      "notes": "এক + classifier -টা. The everyday 'a / one (thing)'. Formal/written: একটি."
    },
    {
      "id": "amader",
      "bn": "আমাদের",
      "tr": "amader",
      "en": "our"
    },
    {
      "id": "tomader",
      "bn": "তোমাদের",
      "tr": "tomader",
      "en": "your (familiar, plural)"
    },
    {
      "id": "bachcha",
      "bn": "বাচ্চা",
      "tr": "bachcha",
      "en": "child"
    },
    {
      "id": "shami",
      "bn": "স্বামী",
      "tr": "shami",
      "en": "husband",
      "notes": "The ব-fola after স is silent."
    },
    {
      "id": "stri",
      "bn": "স্ত্রী",
      "tr": "stri",
      "en": "wife",
      "notes": "Neutral/formal. Colloquially বউ."
    },
    {
      "id": "bou",
      "bn": "বউ",
      "tr": "bou",
      "en": "wife",
      "notes": "Colloquial 'wife'; also 'bride' and 'daughter-in-law'. Also spelled বৌ."
    }
  ],
